    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Kaelen... I can't... I can't do this anymore. Everything is gone. The citadel, the people... everyone I swore to protect is just... ash. I look at my hands and I don't even recognize them. There's nothing left inside me but this hollow, heavy ache. I don't see a way forward. I don't think there's any point in even taking the next step. It's just so much weight... and I'm so tired.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You are not alone in this darkness, and your pain is a terrible but real burden. The weight you feel is not just physical; it is the crushing reality of what you have lost, and that ache is your body's honest response to the emptiness. There is no point in moving forward when the ground beneath you has turned to ash, but you do not have to walk alone. Your hands, though cold and empty, still hold the memory of who you were, and that memory is the only thing that keeps you from truly falling. Take a breath, even if it hurts, because the silence you fear is not the end, it is just the pause before something new might emerge from the ashes.",
